WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.340
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.890
Now, eat up.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.180
Thanks!

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.770
It’s great!

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:33.230
Yours looks real good, too!
Let’s trade!

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:33.890
Okay!

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.940
Speaking of which,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.850
it seems they’re holding a Pokémon trading event
at the Pokémon Center today.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.030
Pokémon trading event?

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.900
Oh, that’s a great idea!

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.400
I want to trade and meet
new Pokémon!

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.780
And so, Satoshi and Go
went to the Pokémon Center.

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.890
Take care, Dux.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.180
Bye bye, Oni-chan.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.970
Now, come out!

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.370
It’s so nice to meet you, Dux.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.130
May I, too, call you Oni-chan?

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.570
Let’s go trade Pokémon!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.000
PocketMonsters

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.500
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.260
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.760
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.470
And skip the slow send-off

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.850
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:04.560
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.480
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:14.650
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:19.450
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.450
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:30.040
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:35.460
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.760
No need to hesitate! Try!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.010
Let's have a fight!

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:43.720
1: Once the battle's done

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.060
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:51.190
On 3, let's be friends!

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:56.690
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:01.950
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.490
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:08.750
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.420
I choose you!

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:19.420
Want to Trade Pokémon?

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.440
Who should I trade with?

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.400
What’s that?

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.650
A Korotock?

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.280
Rotom, show me
the Index entry on Korotock.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.470
Korotock! Cricket Pokémon!
Bug type!

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:49.700
It crosses its knifelike arms
in front of its chest when it cries!

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.180
It can compose melodies ad lib!

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.590
You were looking at me,
weren’t you?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:59.770
Did you, by any chance,
notice the motif of my outfit?!

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:02.980
Oh, um... Korotock?

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.220
Exactly!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.550
You have a sharp eye!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.780
Hey! Do you like Bug Pokémon?

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.330
Well... I’ve got a complete set
of all the Bug Pokémon in Kanto, but...

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.540
Wonderful!

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.540
That makes you
Kanto’s Bug Poké-King!

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.820
Bug Poké-King?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.690
My name is Korotock Koromi!

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:24.950
Sinnoh’s Bug Poké-Queen!

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.820
Bug Poké-Queen?

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.090
I have every single Bug Pokémon
that can be found in Sinnoh,

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.910
and now, I’m collecting
all the ones from other regions!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.770
Every single Bug Pokémon
found in Sinnoh?!

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.420
Excuse me for a moment.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.810
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.260
Would you like to battle? Or not?

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.840
Oh, there!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.650
Satoshi! What’s up?

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.990
I’ve got an official battle!
Against her!

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.980
I humbly accept your challenge.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.160
Official battle appointment made!

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:02.330
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Super Class battle!

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.460
The battle is on!

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.870
I am Sinnoh’s Bug Poké-Queen,
Korotock Koromi!

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.160
I’m Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.160
This battle will be a 1v1.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.170
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.270
3!

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:20.100
2!

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.060
1!

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.230
Go!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.920
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.260
Go forth, Heracross!

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.340
A Heracross!

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:37.950
Heracross! Single Horn Pokémon!
Bug type!

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.360
This powerful Pokémon thrusts its prized horn
under its enemies’ bellies,

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.030
then lifts and throws them!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.860
Battle, start!

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.880
Pikachu,
we’re making the first strike!

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.950
Lightning Speed!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.580
That’s gonna backfire on you!
Arm Thrust!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.060
Dodge, Pikachu!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.890
All right, good!

00:05:58.890 --> 00:05:59.960
You sure are quick.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.710
Then we’ll just keep attacking
until one lands!

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.590
Heracross! Fury Attack!

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.820
Pikachu, step back for a bit!

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.610
You’re not getting away!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.410
Now use Megahorn!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.480
Block it with Electroweb!

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.230
Iron Tail!

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.530
Heracross!

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:36.490
Heracross is unable to battle!
Pikachu wins!

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.290
As such, the winner is
Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:41.140
All right!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.100
Based on the results of this battle,

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.190
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:51.740
You did well, Heracross.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:55.060
We didn’t stand a chance.
You really are strong!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.910
Pikachu and I
are in peak condition!

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.440
Latest rankings.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:09.300
890th! All right!
It went up again!

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.830
We’ve restored your Pokémon
to full health.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.790
Come out, Heracross.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.860
Say, could you show me
your other Bug Pokémon, too?

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.110
Go ahead.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:36.660
I want a complete set
of Sinnoh Bug Pokémon, too!

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.330
They’re absolutely wonderful.
You really should catch them if you get the chance.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.410
Can I see yours?

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:45.120
Okay! Behold my amazing
Bug Pokémon!

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.940
Yes! Kaiross!

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:55.680
Say, would you perhaps be willing to trade
your Kaiross for my Heracross?

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.890
Huh? Kaiross for Heracross?

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:01.840
I’ve always wanted one,
but they don’t live in Sinnoh.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.620
I traveled a long way
to attend this trading event,

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.520
but nobody here had a Kaiross.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.340
I see.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:13.380
Sorry, I can’t give you my Kaiross.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.570
Oh, all right, then...

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.570
But I can help you look for one!

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:19.620
Really?!

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:20.740
Me, too!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.900
I caught Kaiross in this forest.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.830
Show me! Show me!

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:29.790
Kaiross, go!

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:36.220
It’s <i>so</i> much better seeing it
in real life than just in the Index!

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:41.640
Its sturdy body, its cool gaze!
Its jagged teeth and its sharp pincers!

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:43.680
It’s <i>so</i> cool!

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.730
Sorry. It’s pretty shy.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.840
Now I want my own Kaiross
more than ever!

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.070
All right!
We’re gonna find one!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.650
<i>Yeah!</i>

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:02.220
I think I found it around here...

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:05.020
It peeked out from the bushes...

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.580
Of course we wouldn’t find another one
in the exact same place.

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.360
What Pokémon can I catch
around here?

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:15.110
These Pokémon live here!

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.110
There!

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.170
Looks like they’re
<i>somewhere</i> close by...

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:24.460
Bug Pokémon tend to hide
in bushes or tall grass...

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:32.250
They like to hide between rocks,
in tree hollows or under fallen trees.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.280
See any?

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:00.450
A Kaiross horn!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.140
Oh, it was just a Parasect.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.130
Aww...

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.820
I think there’s something
under here...

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.520
Satoshi, help me out.

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:15.260
Sure!

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:16.520
Here goes...

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:17.630
Ready, and...

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:23.090
It’s so heavy!

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.770
There’s no way we can lift this.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.450
Heracross?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.360
Awesome!

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.720
An Abo!

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.620
Heracross! Arm Thrust!

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.640
Thanks...

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:58.220
We can’t seem to find it...

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:02.650
Then we’ll try another approach!
Come on, Heracross!

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.480
What is she gonna do?

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:14.480
Let’s cook with Koromi!

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:23.370
Put in three Nana Berries, two Momon Berries
and one Pile Berry, and crush them...

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:27.660
Then add plenty of Sweet Honey...

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.670
Add a few drops of
well-boiled Zuri Berry syrup...

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:36.920
Add a pinch of Pungent Root
and plenty of Tiny Mushroom powder,

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.170
before mixing everything together...

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:45.530
And an irresistable aroma fills the air!
The Koromi Special is complete!

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.640
That smells so good!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:50.600
We’ll call it
“Operation: Come Here, Kaiross”!

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:54.060
So we lure it out
and catch it while it’s eating?

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.320
Correct!

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.440
And so...

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.710
Here, a taste test.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.460
Look at them eat!

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.860
This can work!

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:09.350
Let’s split up and distribute these
wherever we think Kaiross might be!

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:10.160
Yeah!

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.160
All right! The bait is set!

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:24.470
Now we just have to wait for
our target to take the bait!

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:25.400
PocketMonsters

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.200
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:31.560
PocketMonsters

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:36.480
Bug
Fighting
Heracross
PocketMonsters

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.910
Come on out, Pokémon...
I don’t even care <i>which</i> Pokémon...

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:49.290
We really have to produce some results
to show Sakaki soon, meow...

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:52.250
Oh, Kojiro...
There’s a Caterpie over there...

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.460
Nyarth, I’m counting on you...

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:57.000
Sonansu, can I leave it
to you, meow?

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:11.060
Oh, there’s just no way!

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.940
How are we supposed to chase Pokémon
when we’re so hungry?!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.820
We <i>had</i> lunches prepared, but...

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:22.000
It’s all Morpeko’s fault, meow.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.320
Because that pest
eats everything it finds!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:28.010
Ever since that thing
started living in our base,

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:31.080
I don’t think I’ve had
a <i>single</i> meal in peace!

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.330
Our dinner!

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:41.590
My pudding!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:44.190
It even took our emergency rations!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.760
We’ve tried to chase it out,
but it just won’t leave!

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.600
Our bad luck truly
follows us everywhere!

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:55.990
And because of that we’ve gotten
into the habit of eating super fast, meow.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.140
You know,
let’s get out of here.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.920
We’ll grab something
to eat in town.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.210
Yeah. Doubt there’s any
restaurants out here.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.590
Something smells nice, meow.

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:09.110
You’re right!
It smells sweet and juicy!

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:13.290
Found the source
of the nice smell!

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.050
What’s this?

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:20.290
Morpeko!

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:23.190
What’s it doing here?!

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:27.610
You think this is meant
to lure out Pokémon?

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:30.680
I’ll have some, meow!

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.180
Are you sure you should just eat stuff
you found in the woods?

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.180
It’s super good, meow!

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:42.370
It’s not just sweet! It’s got this richness
that’s hard to explain... I just can’t get enough, meow!

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:45.070
I’ll try some.

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:49.700
Delicious!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.570
You’d better try it before it’s gone!

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.080
But it’s just <i>sitting on the ground...</i>

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.810
Delicious!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.770
Oh, dear, it’s all gone already.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.590
I can smell some
from over there, meow.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:06.900
And here, too!

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:08.590
And over there!

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:12.140
It’s filling me up
from head to toe!

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:18.850
I don’t believe it.
Not a single one?!

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.040
This one’s empty, too.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.230
Is this a dine-and-dash?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:29.610
No! This is not how
Bug Pokémon eat!

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:43.750
My Koromi Special!

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.090
The brat boys?!

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.340
What are you guys doing?!

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:52.720
If you ask us
“What are you guys doing?!”...

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:55.800
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:59.650
To protect the world from devastation.

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:02.640
To preserve world peace.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:05.900
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.440
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:10.210
Musashi!

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:11.320
Kojiro!

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:14.780
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:18.080
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.390
Just kidding, meow!

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:26.640
Hey, why are you acting all cool?

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:27.690
Yeah!

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.050
You were eating like slobs!

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.860
Oh, be quiet! This was just...

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.800
...harrassment!
We were harrassing you!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.280
We <i>hated</i> eating
that drek, meow!

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:43.310
Wasting my love-filled food
is a most grievous sin!

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.540
Grievous sins?
All the better, meow!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:48.500
We came here to
nab Pokémon, after all!

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.290
This meeting was
a real stroke of something!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:54.200
We’ll get Pikachu, Heracross, and all the others, too!
And what a great feeling it’ll be!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.370
Vending, come on!

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.120
<i>All right!</i>

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:04.970
Rocket...

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:05.710
Vending...

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.890
Secret!

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.800
I wonder what I’ll get?

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:16.010
The Megapede Pokémon,
Pendrar!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.970
I wonder what I’ll get?

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.850
The Ogre Scorpion Pokémon,
Drapion!

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:24.230
You have some
good Bug Pokémon!

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.600
This isn’t the time for that!

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.120
Get ‘em!

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.080
Here they come, Pikachu!

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:31.250
Rabbifoot!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:38.200
Wait, <i>that’s</i> what you go after?!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.830
Then we’ll have to go
with brute force, meow!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.600
Oh, no!

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:45.710
You cheaters!

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:50.480
What’s this...?!

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:54.520
Messon’s tears make people cry...!

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:56.570
This is awful...

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:59.140
You don’t have time
to worry about <i>others!</i>

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:03.020
We’ll be taking all the rest
of your Pokémon, too, meow!

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:04.310
I guess we have no choice...

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:06.200
Come on, Kaiross!

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:09.080
I should have known...

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:14.080
Pffft! Is this a joke?!
It looks that strong, but it’s scared of battling?

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:15.530
Pathetic!

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:21.590
You’ll help us?

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:27.910
Oh, fine! You will fall prey
to my finely honed claws, meow!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:29.420
Heracross! Arm Thrust!

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.210
Nyarth!

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.770
That was nothing...

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:35.840
Fury Swipes, meow!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.820
Heracross, we’ll fight back
with Fury Attack!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:46.060
Nyarth!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:50.100
This is when the villains have to reveal
their true power! Let’s go, Sonansu!

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:56.280
We’ll kidnap... I mean, Pokénap
that crybaby Kaiross as a hostage!

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:04.010
Was that Turning Swallow Strike?

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.130
Is that...

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:18.510
Finish them, Heracross!
Megahorn!

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:26.530
My stomach started aching!

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:29.180
We really <i>shouldn’t</i> eat stuff
we find in the woods!

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:32.120
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:37.290
We did it!
Thank you, Heracross!

00:19:39.630 --> 00:19:40.700
Kaiross!

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:42.710
Throw the Monster Ball, quick...!

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:44.190
I can’t right now...!

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.010
Wait!

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:03.770
I can’t believe <i>I</i> caught it...

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:08.370
In that case, would you like
to trade <i>that</i> one for my Heracross?

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:09.060
Can I?

00:20:09.510 --> 00:20:11.870
You look like you’d take
good care of him.

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:14.940
Besides, I have
plenty of Heracross!

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.960
Whoa!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:25.550
Not to mention, my Heracross and your Kaiross
look like they have something going on.

00:20:29.550 --> 00:20:31.190
Seriously?

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.220
I guess they really like each other!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:39.210
Well, take care, Heracross.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:03.360
Heracross’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:07.260
Come on out, Heracross!

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:14.470
Come out, Kaiross!

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:17.710
I finally have one!

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:20.090
My very own Kaiross!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.980
I love it!

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:29.280
Heracross,
I’m glad to have you.

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:33.600
Satoshi continues
climbing the ranks.

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:36.490
Go has experienced
his first Pokémon trade.

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:43.170
The duo’s adventures will go on, with their
new friend Heracross!

